@startuml product-autonomy-authority-boundary
title Product Autonomy Authority Boundary ; per ADR-ES-017 §4 + §6

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Autonomous Product" as AP
class "Product Objective" as Obj
class "Authority" as Auth
class "Policy" as Pol
class "Constraints" as Con
class "Governance" as Gov
class "Escalation" as Esc

AP --> Obj : pursues
AP --> Auth : operates-within
AP --> Pol : governed-by
AP --> Con : constrained-by
AP --> Gov : operates-within
AP --> Esc : escalates-to

note bottom of AP
  Per ADR-ES-017 §4, autonomous progression is bounded by
  six fences: Objective -> Authority -> Policy -> Constraints
  -> Governance -> Escalation.
  Autonomy means bounded independent progression, NOT
  unrestricted operation.
end note

@enduml
